<title>USA: NY Gov defends new FY 1998 budget pact as prudent.</title>
<headline>NY Gov defends new FY 1998 budget pact as prudent.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York Gov. George Pataki, who unveiled a much-delayed budget pact only to have fiscal monitors immediately attack it, Wednesday defended the plan, saying the state could afford $4.75 billion of tax cuts.</p>
<p>Pataki told reporters at a briefing that the approximately $67 billion budget agreement for fiscal 1998, which still must be enacted by the legislature, was prudent, and did not rely on unrealistic projections for Wall Street firm's profits.</p>
</text>
